[[File:S1E02 Dante Freelancer Redcap.jpg|thumb|Dante and his Freelancer rush into battle]]
Dante invoked his Freelancer on the streets of Venice to fight against two [[Suits]] and their [[Redcap]] [[Titans]]. {{source|The Casterwill Client}} Dante later invoked his Freelancer in the [[Paris Catacombs]] to fight [[Grier]]'s [[Breaker]]. {{source|Divide and Conquer}}

Dante summoned his Freelancer in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] to defend against [[Klaus]] and his men whilst trying to escape with the [[Sceptre of Nefertiti]]. Freelancer shielded attacks from the Suits and three [[Enforcer]] [[Titans]]. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}} Dante invoked Freelancer alongside [[Solwing]] and [[Caliban]] in [[Klaus' bookshop]] to fight [[Brahe]] and the Suits, giving the team time to escape with the [[Bottle of Djinn]]. {{source|The Bookshop Hunter}} Whilst fighting Klaus' forces on the rooftops of the [[Castle of Vlad Dracul]], Dante invoked Freelancer to fight off a [[Bonelasher]]. {{source|The Vampire Loses Its Fangs}}

Dante and Lok both summoned their Freelancers on the way to the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]] to fight against [[Ammit Heart-Eater]] and [[Jokoul]]. {{source|Memory Lane}}

[[File:S1E02 Lok Freelancer.png|thumb|Lok feels the telepathic communication after invoking his Freelancer for the first time]]
When [[Lok Lambert]] first bonded with the Freelancer Amulet that Dante Vale gave him, Lok saw glimpses of his future with the Titan. Both Dante Vale and Lok Lambert have used Freelancer Titans in their battles against [[the Organization]], beginning with Lok's first encounter with the world of Titans. {{source|The Casterwill Client}} Upon joining the [[Huntik Foundation]], Freelancer became one of Lok's main Titans used to fight against many [[the Organization|Organization]] agents over the course of his adventures.

Lok and Dante both summoned their Freelancers on the way to the [[Mausoleum of Sir Lancelot]] to fight against [[Ammit Heart-Eater]] and [[Jokoul]]. {{source|Memory Lane}}

Lok was seen scanning his Freelancer on his [[Holotome]] during one of [[LeBlanche]]'s classes. {{source|Cave of the Casterwills}} Lok summoned his Freelancer outside the [[Cathedral of Notre Dame]] to fight against [[Clements]]' Freelancer, [[Ironsquire]] and [[Hoplite]] Titans. After seeing Lok in danger, his Freelancer threw his lance at Hoplite, before being knocked to the floor by Ironsquire. He was then held down by Clements' Freelancer and defeated by Ironsquire. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}
[[File:S2E36 Lok gives Den Freelancer.png|thumb|Lok gives his Freelancer to [[Den Fears]]]]
Lok eventually gave the Amulet to the newer Seeker and member of the team, [[Den Fears]]. Den then later used Freelancer to fight his brother [[Harrison Fears]]. After an intense battle, Freelancer was able to defeat [[Hitokiri]]. {{source|Boys Will Be Seekers}} Den later used Freelancer in [[Hamelin Cathedral]] to fight alongside Powerbonded Lindorm against the [[Gremlow]] Titans. {{source|Gremlow Infestation}}
